Just a few random ideas, some related to the water discussion, some
not.

New potion: Potion of Alka-Seltzer.  Un-Satiates you.  Goes well with
dragon corpses.  Message when drinking would be ``This tastes fizzy.''
Blessed/normal/cursed affects degree of hunger you feel after quaffing
(maybe cursed has the opposite effect, e.g. ``You feel bloated.'').

New potion: Potion of Dramamine (sp?).  Can't become confused or
stunned for x number of turns after drinking it.  Message if not
already confused/stunned:  ``You feel stable.''

(Since the last two are both available in drug stores, maybe a new
class of objects called pharmacueticals (sp?).  Could include cold
medicine for curing sickness, NoDoze for temporary sleep resistance,
etc.  Also some negative drugs, which might lower intelligence or
other stats, cause sickness, maybe even be addictive.  Should be more
rare than potions and more expensive.)

Related to the water discussion:

Some people have suggested variable depth pools, etc.  Along with
that...

New tool: Snorkel.  Apply within a turn or two of falling into a
shallow pool and allows you to live (armor, etc. still rusts).
Useless in a deep pool, or the moats.

New ring: Ring of water breathing.  Like the snorkel, but also good
for deeper pools.  Blessed version might also protect your armor.
Cursed version might force you to breathe *only* water, so you
``drown'' outside the pool.  Water breathing could also be an
intrinsic, perhaps obtainable from eating Rust monsters.

Modified monster: Kraken.  Already exist, but make it more like the
mythical kraken.  While standing next to one, it has some chance every
turn of pulling you under the water.  Levitation or water-walking
boots won't save you, but the ring of water breathing will.  Fighting
under water should be slower than fighting on land, so the kraken
should get more hits on you while you're under water than while you
are fighting from the floor.  If you kill the kraken while standing on
solid ground, there should be a some kraken leaves (arms? tentacles?)
laying around.  Eating these may give intrinsic water breathing.  This
monster would help balance the advantages of the above two artifacts.

